% there is
% a natural number
% an integer $n=n(a,b)$ such that, in $G(X,r)$,
% we have  $a* (a*(\ldots a*(a* b)))=0$ (where $a$ occurs $n$ times and $b$ occurs once in
% this equality
% %equation),
% then $(X,r)$ is the trivial solution.
%In particular, if  $G(X,r)$ is a left nilpotent left brace then
%$(X,r)$ is the trivial solution.
